# Server of the network check with a browser client (see ../run.mjs --browser): the browser build needs
# many seconds to load, so every script waits much longer than the native variants before it prints what
# it sees, giving all bodies time to come to rest first. The server must print while the browser client
# is still connected: Chrome closes its session cleanly on exit, so the server would remove that
# client's player body at once, and a native client leaves silently (the server notices much later).
wait 3300
# (No client count here: the native client has already left by now. That both clients took part shows in
# the bodies: net_a came from the native client and net_b from the browser client.)
net.bodies
net.stats
# Traffic budget (measured: about 60-120 KB sent, 5-30 KB received) with 3x headroom, and no refusals:
# every client here is honest, so any refusal is a bug in the client or in the limits.
assert.net_bytes_below sent 400000
assert.net_bytes_below received 100000
assert.net_refusals_at_most 0
quit
